<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9107" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">collūdĭum</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conl-</span></b> ), ii, n.
		colludo (post-class.). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A sporting</i>, <i>playing
			together</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">delphinorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sol. 12</span></i>
			; so <i><span class="en">Symm. Ep. 3,
			5</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A secret</i>, <i>deceptive
				understanding</i>, <i>collusion</i>, esp. in
			justice, <i><span class="en">Amm. 18, 5, 1</span></i>; Cod. Th. 9,
			42, 20; 11, 42, 7; <i><span class="en">Symm. Ep. 4, 20</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
